# THE SLUMS: the city still runs its atmosphere plant, and the smog dome it makes
# is thick enough that the street never gets the sun (`BiomeDef.sky_shut`,
# src/render/sky_light.gd LID_*, src/systems/11_dome.gd).
#
# What this proves, in order: the landscape is reachable and names itself; it is
# under a lid at every hour; and THE HOUR BARELY REACHES THE STREET.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/slums-dome.tour --seed=7

# --- the control, first, and it is the whole instrument -------------------
#
# The coast is where this game's night was calibrated (SkyLight.NIGHT_AMBIENT was
# measured on its mid-value grass, and `night_sky` 1.0 is its). So the coast's own
# noon-against-midnight is what a day costs in a landscape with nothing over it,
# measured in this same run, on this same machine, under this same load.
place coast
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 1.4
shot 01-coast-noon with land:coast
hour 0
wait 1.4
shot 02-coast-midnight with land:coast

# --- the same day, under the dome ------------------------------------------
place slums
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 1.6
# The lid is over this place at noon. `dome` is computed off the live blended
# shares the sky composed with (11_dome.tour_seen), never off a latch, so it
# cannot answer for a lid the player walked out of ten minutes ago.
await dome 6
shot 03-slums-noon with land:slums
hour 0
wait 1.6
shot 04-slums-midnight with land:slums

# --- THE CLAIM --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A whole day and a whole night cost this street LESS than they cost the coast.
#
# It is deliberately relational and not an absolute bar, for the reason
# docs/LOOK.md gives in as many words: an absolute number here would be pinned to
# how much the world animates — tufts, cloud shade, the player's own breathing —
# and would go red for the weather while saying nothing whatever about the lid.
# Both pairs are captured inside ONE run, so a busy machine moves both equally
# and cancels (docs/LOOK.md, "a difference measured WITHIN one run is safe where
# a difference measured ACROSS runs is not").
#
# NO SLACK IS GIVEN. If the dome ever stops holding the hour off the street this
# goes red, and that is the entire point of the file: the number it is held to is
# a property of the coast, so it follows the game rather than drifting from it.
same 03-slums-noon 04-slums-midnight no_more_than 01-coast-noon 02-coast-midnight

# --- and where the lid is torn ---------------------------------------------
#
# `until` and not `await`: a tear is dealt on a 26-tile grid (Dome.CELL) and the
# pool it lays walks across the street over the day, so whether one is within
# reach of this particular spawn at this particular hour is a property of the
# seed and not something the landscape owes anybody. A tour that FAILED here
# would be asserting something this file cannot honestly promise — and a green
# step that proved nothing is worse than a red one.
hour 11
wait 1.2
until shaft 8
shot 05-light-through-a-tear with land:slums
